# What `docker build` leaves out of the context for both images (apps/api/Dockerfile, apps/web/Dockerfile): what the
# build makes again (dependencies, generated code, build output), local secrets, and what no image needs. A pattern
# without **/ matches at the context's root alone: `next build` reads apps/web/.env* and copies .env and
# .env.production into the image, so every .env is left out at any depth (the image smoke checks that none is there).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.log
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/src/generated
**/coverage
**/.vitest
**/*.tsbuildinfo
apps/web/public/icons
apps/web/public/sw.js
apps/web/test-results
apps/web/playwright-report
.git
.github
.husky
.vscode
.claude
.claude-flow
.superpowers
docs
